        "branch": "whole",
        "query": "Set up a Next.js App Router project for our CLI tool marketplace \"TerminalVault\" — I want the landing page to feature an animated ASCII art splash banner that plays a retro terminal-style boot sequence animation (think old CRT startup with our logo assembling character by character) before revealing the main content using server components and streaming. Also, I need to wire up several backend integrations for managing tool listings — we'll need JIRA for tracking submission reviews, Slack for notifying maintainers, and Google Docs for generating changelogs — so please discover what MCP tools are available for each of those services and map out the full workflow for how a new tool submission flows through the pipeline. For the Next.js piece specifically, I want to understand the best way to handle the transition from the ASCII splash animation to the streamed server component content using Suspense boundaries, and whether I should use route intercepting or parallel routes for the tool detail modals.",
